    {
      "id": "b000001",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 1,
      "end_line": 1,
      "raw": "# HLSHello\n",
      "level": 1,
      "title": "HLSHello"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000002",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 2,
      "end_line": 2,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 3,
      "end_line": 3,
      "raw": "`crc8.cpp` is the actual C++23 synthesis input. The builder lowers the bounded CRC-8 algorithm to a typed dataflow and SystemVerilog. `board.v` connects its generated `crc_kernel` ready/valid interface to a counter and LED. `ice40.pcf` is specifically for the iCEstick HX1K TQ144 clock/LED pins.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000004",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 4,
      "end_line": 4,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 5,
      "end_line": 5,
      "raw": "Run a portable RTL build with the example manifest:\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000006",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 6,
      "end_line": 6,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000007",
      "kind": "fenced_code",
      "start_line": 7,
      "end_line": 9,
      "raw": "```sh\niisdk-builder build --manifest examples/HLSHello/iiSDKBuilder.json --sdk-root /path/to/SDK\n```\n",
      "language": "sh",
      "code": "iisdk-builder build --manifest examples/HLSHello/iiSDKBuilder.json --sdk-root /path/to/SDK\n",
      "closed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "b000008",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 10,
      "end_line": 10,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 11,
      "end_line": 11,
      "raw": "The manifest uses `clang++` and `yosys` from the kit environment. To generate an iCE40 image, choose `implementation: ice40`, `part: hx1k`, `family: tq144`, `top: hls_board`, the wrapper and constraints, and a clock period of 83333 ps. The same emitted SystemVerilog can be implemented through the Vivado or Quartus adapters with their actual part/constraint/tool settings.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000010",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 12,
      "end_line": 12,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000011",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 13,
      "end_line": 13,
      "raw": "See [HLS](../../docs/HLS.md) for the exact supported C++ subset. The FPGA contains gates and registers; Core manages build-time process ownership on the host. Device programming is a separate explicit step.\n"
    }
  ],
